(git ignores this leading text.)

- Carb split HP1 on a phone without AutoISF is scaled by the profile: IOB x ISF and COB x ISF / IC (was 1 mmol per U and
  1 mmol per 12 g), so a bolus that matches its carbs cancels out. Right after a 6.70 U bolus the old formula read HP1 about
  3.4 under BG and held the split at every 2-minute check ("HP1 below 4.0 mmol/L"). Without a profile, the old formula.
- A carb split part is not held for "HP1 below 4.0" while BG is 7.0 mmol/L or more and both deltas are rising. The other
  split checks (glucose, insulinReq, walking) still apply. The falling-trend caution keeps the old HP1 formula.

